# Test: OSPFv2 Extended Prefix LSA decode (RFC 7684, spec-ospf-ext-4).
#
# VALIDATES: an Extended Prefix opaque LSA (Opaque Type 7) encodes, decodes with a valid Fletcher checksum, splits its Link State ID to Opaque Type 7, and its body decodes to an Extended Prefix TLV (the CLI decode path).
# PREVENTS: a byte-order slip in the LS-ID split or a mis-padded Extended Prefix TLV body.

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=go test -v ./internal/plugins/ospf -run TestOSPFExtDecodeFunctional -count=1:timeout=60s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=PASS
